{"authority":"LOCAL_SYNTHETIC","bundle_hash":"87e4416d72408979a341bdb80581201bbd7306be4bb1d81157693f641025ec4e","disposition":"Reviewed net-asset attribution; every ownership subparagraph retained","quote":"3.4 When ascertaining the value of net assets of an SPI, intermediaries may take into\naccount one or more of the following –\n(a)\n\nthe value of assets and liabilities held on –\n(i)\n\nan SPI’s own account;\n\n(ii)\n\njoint account with the SPI’s associate;\n\n(iii) joint account owned by the SPI with one or more persons other than the\nSPI’s associate, to the value equivalent to the SPI’s share on the joint\naccount as specified in a written agreement among the account holders or,\nan equal share of the joint account in the absence of such agreement;\n(b)\n\n","reviewer_id":"synthetic.meaning","rule_ids":["spi.financial"],"span_id":"spi.annex1.3.4"}